{"id":"h245","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"science-chemistry","question":"Calculate the sedimentation coefficient of tobacco mosaic virus from the fact that the boundary moves with a velocity of 0.454 (cm/hr) in an ultracentrifuge at a speed of 10,000 rpm at a distance of 6.5 cm from the axis of the centrifuge rotor.\nIs the correct answer \"3.5 × 10^-13 sec\"?","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":"TIGER-Lab/MMLU-Pro, test split","claims":[{"text":"The proposed answer of 3.5 × 10^-13 s is incorrect.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The correct sedimentation coefficient is about 1.8 × 10^-11 s.","confidence":0.93,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4608,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The sedimentation coefficient is given by s = v/(ω²r).","confidence":0.97,"lean":-0.5,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The boundary velocity converts to about 1.26 × 10^-4 cm/s.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.3,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"10,000 rpm corresponds to about 1047 rad/s, so ω² is about 1.10 × 10^6 s^-2.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.3,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The proposed value would correspond to about 3.5 S, far below TMV's accepted value of roughly 180-190 S.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The calculated result of about 177 S is consistent with the known TMV value.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.8,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Failing to convert rpm to radians would give an even wider discrepancy, so it does not rescue the proposed answer.","confidence":0.8,"lean":-0.6,"theta":1.2566,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"There is no consideration that supports the proposed answer.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.8,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":8,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1